root@9749b62daacf:/app/arrow# cat /app/arrow/notes_for_testing.txt
Arrow Library - Date/Time Manipulation Library

Key Functions to Test:

1. arrow.get() - Main parsing function
   - Parse various date/time formats from strings
   - Handle timestamps (int, float)
   - Parse datetime objects
   - Handle timezone expressions
   - Test with malformed input, edge cases

2. arrow.now() / arrow.utcnow() - Current time functions
   - Test with different timezones

3. Arrow.format() - Formatting functions
   - Format to various string representations
   - Test with different locales

4. Arrow parsing (parser.py)
   - DateTimeParser.parse() - parse date strings with format strings
   - Test various format tokens
   - Handle edge cases and malformed inputs

5. Arrow.humanize() - Human-readable time differences
   - Test with different granularities

6. Arrow arithmetic operations
   - shift(), replace(), floor(), ceil()
   - Range operations

Fuzzing Strategy:
- Focus on get() with random string inputs (most likely to have parsing bugs)
- Test format() with random format strings
- Test parser with various date/time string formats
- Include timezone handling edge cases
- Test with invalid/malformed inputs to find crashes
